      "dom_id": "question-79026",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "What is the diameter of a circle if its area is $9\\pi \\,{\\text{km}}^{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the area of a circle is $A=\\pi {r}^{2}$, where $r$ is the radius. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 9\\pi  & =\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 9\\cancel{\\pi } & =\\cancel{\\pi }{r}^{2} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =9 \\\\ r & =3\\,\\text{km}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the diameter is\n\n$$\nd=2\\cdot r=2\\cdot 3=6\\,\\text{km}.\n$$",
